}", "answer": "function findDuplicates(arr) {
  const seen = new Set();
  const dupes = new Set();
  for (const item of arr) {
    if (seen.has(item)) dupes.add(item);
    else seen.add(item);
  }
  return [...dupes];
}", "explanation": "A Set tracks values already seen; any value encountered again is added to a separate duplicates set, and converting that set back to an array gives each duplicate exactly once.", "concepts": ["duplicates", "set"]}

