{"question": "Implement a `useDebounce` custom hook that returns a debounced version of a value after a given delay.", "starter_code": "function useDebounce(value, delay) {
  // return debounced value
}", "answer": "function useDebounce(value, delay) {
  const [debounced, setDebounced] = useState(value);
  useEffect(() => {
    const t = setTimeout(() => setDebounced(value), delay);
    return () => clearTimeout(t);
  }, [value, delay]);
  return debounced;
}", "explanation": "Each time `value` changes, the previous pending timeout is cleared before a new one is set, so `debounced` only updates once the value has stopped changing for `delay` milliseconds.", "concepts": ["custom hook", "debounce", "useeffect"]}

